## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design privacy-preserving, offline-first collaborative systems at scale. It tests technical understanding of cryptographic protocols, peer-to-peer networking, CRDT algorithms, and cost-benefit analysis while considering regulatory compliance and user experience constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving collaborative editing
- CRDT convergence and conflict-free resolution
- Peer-to-peer mesh topology and infrastructure costs
- End-to-end encryption with lifecycle key management
- Compliance logging and audit trail requirements
- Performance trade-offs between latency and device resource consumption

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple OR-Set CRDT merge (illustrative)
function mergeORSet(A, B) {
  const merged = new Set([...A.added, ...B.added]);
  [...A.removed, ...B.removed].forEach(item => merged.delete(item));
  return merged;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to reason about on-device ML tradeoffs, privacy, federated updates, and cost implications for a beginner-level feature in widely-used apps.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference and model sizing
- Federated learning basics and backend costs
- Energy and latency budgets for mobile feeds
- Privacy/compliance and user consent flows
- Rollout strategies and offline fallback
- Drift/maintenance and break-even horizon

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-cost estimator (not used in production)
function estimateCBA(modelMB, latencyMs, energyPerInference, users) {
  const deviceCost = modelMB * 1.2;
  const latencyCost = latencyMs * 0.5;
  const energyCost = energyPerInference * 60;
  const backendCost = 0.1;
  return deviceCost + latencyCost + energyCost + backendCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you estimate user consent overhead in practice?
- What metrics signal drift in a deployed on-device ranking model?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to translate usage into a cost-benefit framework for a privacy-preserving, offline-first sync feature, including storage, energy, and cloud costs.

## Key Concepts

- Data sizing and retention policies
- On-device energy and encryption overhead
- Cloud storage/egress pricing and scaling
- Privacy/compliance considerations and opt-in flows
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost({clipsPerDay, bytesPerClip, retentionDaysCloud, users, costPerGB}) {
  const perUserMB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * 365 / (1024 * 1024);
  const cloudGB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * retentionDaysCloud * 365 / (1024 * 1024 * 1024);
  const monthlyCost = (cloudGB * costPerGB) / 12;
  const totalMonthly = monthlyCost * users;
  return { perUserMB, cloudGB, totalMonthly };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the CBA for user growth and volatility in clip frequency?
- What privacy/consent controls would you expose, and how would they impact costs and ROI?

## Why This Is Asked

Explores cost trade-offs of on-device privacy-preserving telemetry at scale, balancing data minimization with operational transparency.

## Key Concepts

- On-device aggregation and secure aggregation
- Data minimization vs. data utility
- Compliance costs vs. backend savings
- Phased rollout and break-even metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: merge deltas with secure aggregation placeholder
function aggregateDeltas(deltas, state) {
  // secure-aggregate-friendly merge
  const merged = deltas.reduce((acc, d) => acc + d.value, 0);
  state.total += merged;
  return state;
}
```

